  "id": "RAW_63cd406cb4",
  "title": "Anthropic 发布 Claude Fable 5.1 与 Claude Mythos 5.1：Terminal-Bench-Science 评分 52.6% 且缓存读取成本降低 75%",
  "url": "https://www.marktechpost.com/2026/09/01/anthropic-releases-claude-fable-5-1-and-claude-mythos-5-1-52-6-on-terminal-bench-science-and-75-cheaper-cache-reads/",
  "date": "2026-09-02 04:30:22",
  "author": "Asif Razzaq",
  "siteName": "MarkTechPost",
  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"h-\">Anthropic has released Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1, three months after the Fable 5 line shipped in June 2026. The two are the same underlying model behind different safeguard layers. Fable 5.1 is generally available as <code>claude-fable-5-1</code>; Mythos 5.1 stays restricted to vetted organizations. Both carry a 1M token context window and 128K max output tokens, with adaptive thinking always on. The headline capability number is 52.6% on Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1, against 24.7% for Fable 5 and 29.0% for Opus 5. The headline commercial number is a 75% cut to cache reads, from $1.00 to $0.25 per million tokens, which Anthropic measures as roughly 25% lower cost on typical workloads and up to 45% on agentic ones. Base input and output pricing is unchanged at $10 and $50 per million.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-is-it-deployable\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Is it deployable?</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Yes, </strong><a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/claude-fable-and-mythos-5-1\">Claude Fable 5.1</a> is generally available as <code>claude-fable-5-1</code> on the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, Claude Platform on AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Foundry. Claude Mythos 5.1 is not: it is restricted to vetted US organizations inside <a href=\"https://anthropic.com/glasswing\">Project Glasswing</a>.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-the-benchmark-numbers\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The benchmark numbers</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1, an agentic scientific research benchmark, Fable 5.1 scores 52.6% against 29.0% for Opus 5, 24.7% for Fable 5, and 22.4% for GPT-5.6 Sol. Anthropic reports a standard error of 3.5 to 4.5 points per model, so treat the margin, not the ranking, with care.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On Terminal-Bench 4.0, Fable 5.1 reaches 55.8% and Mythos 5.1 reaches 60.9%. The gap between two identical models is the cost of safeguard interventions, which is an unusually honest disclosure. Elsewhere: CursorBench 3.2.0 at 73.4%, Humanity’s Last Exam at 60.9% without tools and 65.0% with tools, AutomationBench at 31.4%, OSWorld 2.0 at 41.7% strict, and GDPval-AA v2 at 1853.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-where-the-cost-cut-comes-from\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Where the cost cut comes from</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Base input and output pricing is unchanged. Cache reads drop 75%, from $1.00 to $0.25 per million tokens, which is 0.025 times base input against 0.1 on every other Claude model. Anthropic measures roughly 25% lower cost on typical workloads and up to about 45% on context-heavy agentic ones. Batch processing is $5 and $25 per million tokens.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-three-breaking-changes-teams-will-hit\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Three breaking changes teams will hit</strong></h2>\n  <ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li><strong>Forced tool use is gone</strong>: <code>tool_choice</code> set to <code>any</code> or <code>tool</code> returns a 400. Use <code>auto</code> with strict tool use or structured outputs instead.</li>\n   <li><strong>Thinking blocks are model-bound</strong>: Fable 5.1 reads earlier models’ thinking, but no earlier model reads its own. Router and fallback setups lose reasoning when they switch down.</li>\n   <li><strong>Editing earlier turns invalidates thinking blocks</strong>: Injecting and deleting per-turn reminders, or rebuilding the <code>system</code> or <code>tools</code> array mid-conversation, now errors. The check is enforced for accounts created on or after August 31, 2026. The fixes are turn-scoped system messages and server-side context editing.</li>\n  </ol>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Additive changes: per-message effort, turn-scoped system messages, and <code>thinking.display: \"updates\"</code> are all in beta behind headers. Content provenance is not optional, with a statistical text watermark on all output and C2PA credentials on files.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Anthropic also documents real regressions. Parallel tool calling is more variable, so agent loops may issue one call per turn where Fable 5 batched several. The model narrates less, answers from memory more often at low effort, and prefers whole-file rewrites over targeted edits.</p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-safeguards-and-science\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Safeguards and science</strong></h2>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cyber safeguards now permit vulnerability discovery but not exploit development, cutting interventions in Claude Code by roughly 60% per session. Biology safeguards fire 85% less often on benign requests. Penetration testing, exploit generation, and binary-based vulnerability scanning still redirect to Opus.</p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On research, Mythos 5.1 designed protein binders with roughly 50% hit rate across 12 targets against a 10 to 15% norm, Fable 5.1 built a <a href=\"https://zenodo.org/records/22164484\">Venus elevation map</a> at 2 to 3 km resolution, and custom GPU kernels sped up seven open-source genomics models by up to 2.5x.</p>\n  <iframe class=\"lazyload\" id=\"mtp-fable51-frame\" srcdoc=\"&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;\n&lt;html lang=&quot;en&quot;&gt;\n&lt;head&gt;\n&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot;&gt;\n&lt;meta name=&quot;viewport&quot; content=&quot;width=device-width, initial-scale=1&quot;&gt;\n&lt;title&gt;Claude Fable 5.1 explainer&lt;/title&gt;\n&lt;style&gt;\n  body#mtpfx51{\n    --ink:#141413; --panel:#1D1C1A; --panel2:#252320;\n    --line:#38342E; --cream:#F0EEE6; --mute:#A29C92;\n    --clay:#D97757; --clay-d:#B95C3F; --sand:#E3D9C6;\n    margin:0!important;background:#141413!important;color:#F0EEE6!important;\n    font-family:ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Inter,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\n    -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}\n  #mtpfx51 *{box-sizing:border-box}\n  #mtpfx51 .fx{max-width:940px;margin:0 auto;padding:22px 18px 16px}\n  #mtpfx51 .hd{border-left:3px solid var(--clay)!important;padding-left:14px;margin-bottom:18px}\n  #mtpfx51 .hd h2{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:22px;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:-.02em;\n    line-height:1.25;color:#F0EEE6!important}\n  #mtpfx51 .hd p{margin:0;font-size:13.5px;color:#A29C92!important;line-height:1.5}\n  #mtpfx51 .tabs{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-bottom:14px}\n  #mtpfx51 .tab{background:transparent!important;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;\n    color:#A29C92!important;padding:8px 13px;border-radius:999px;font-size:12.5px;\n    cursor:pointer;font-family:inherit;transition:background .18s,color .18s,border-color .18s}\n  #mtpfx51 .tab:hover{color:#F0EEE6!important;border-color:#4A443C!important}\n  #mtpfx51 .tab[aria-selected=&quot;true&quot;]{background:var(--clay)!important;\n    border-color:var(--clay)!important;color:#17110E!important;font-weight:600}\n  #mtpfx51 .tab:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--sand);outline-offset:2px}\n  #mtpfx51 .pane{display:none;background:var(--panel)!important;\n    border:1px solid var(--line)!important;border-radius:12px;padding:18px}\n  #mtpfx51 .pane.on{display:block}\n  #mtpfx51 h3{margin:0 0 4px;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;color:#F0EEE6!important}\n  #mtpfx51 .sub{margin:0 0 14px;font-size:12.5px;color:#A29C92!important;line-height:1.55}\n  #mtpfx51 .note{margin:14px 0 0;font-size:11.5px;color:#A29C92!important;line-height:1.55;\n    border-top:1px solid var(--line)!important;padding-top:10px}\n\n  #mtpfx51 .wire{width:100%;height:150px}\n  #mtpfx51 .flow{stroke-dasharray:5 7;animation:mtpfxdash 1.4s linear infinite}\n  @keyframes mtpfxdash{to{stroke-dashoffset:-24}}\n  #mtpfx51 .gates{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:10px;margin-bottom:12px}\n  #mtpfx51 .gate{background:var(--panel2)!important;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;\n    border-radius:10px;padding:13px;cursor:pointer;text-align:left;color:#F0EEE6!important;\n    font-family:inherit;transition:border-color .2s,transform .2s}\n  #mtpfx51 .gate:hover{transform:translateY(-2px);border-color:#4A443C!important}\n  #mtpfx51 .gate[aria-pressed=&quot;true&quot;]{border-color:var(--clay)!important;\n    box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--clay) inset}\n  #mtpfx51 .gate b{display:block;font-size:13.5px;margin-bottom:4px}\n  #mtpfx51 .gate span{font-size:11.5px;color:#A29C92!important;line-height:1.5}\n  #mtpfx51 .detail{background:var(--panel2)!important;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;\n    border-radius:10px;padding:14px;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.65;min-height:96px;\n    color:#F0EEE6!important}\n  #mtpfx51 .detail ul{margin:6px 0 0;padding-left:17px}\n  #mtpfx51 .detail li{margin-bottom:4px}\n\n  #mtpfx51 .chips{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:5px;margin-bottom:14px}\n  #mtpfx51 .chip{background:var(--panel2)!important;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;\n    color:#A29C92!important;padding:6px 11px;border-radius:6px;font-size:11.5px;\n    cursor:pointer;font-family:inherit}\n  #mtpfx51 .chip[aria-pressed=&quot;true&quot;]{background:var(--clay)!important;color:#17110E!important;\n    border-color:var(--clay)!important;font-weight:600}\n  #mtpfx51 .row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:112px 1fr 56px;align-items:center;\n    gap:10px;margin-bottom:9px}\n  #mtpfx51 .nm{font-size:12px;color:#A29C92!important}\n  #mtpfx51 .track{background:#2C2926!important;border-radius:4px;height:19px;overflow:hidden}\n  #mtpfx51 .fill{height:100%;width:0;border-radius:4px;background:#4E4941;\n    transition:width .75s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)}\n  #mtpfx51 .fill.lead{background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--clay-d),var(--clay))}\n  #mtpfx51 .val{font-size:12.5px;text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;\n    color:#F0EEE6!important}\n\n  #mtpfx51 .slab{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;\n    font-size:12.5px;margin-bottom:8px}\n  #mtpfx51 .slab b{font-size:19px;color:var(--clay)!important;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n  #mtpfx51 input[type=range]{width:100%;accent-color:#D97757;margin:0 0 16px}\n  #mtpfx51 .cmp{display:grid;grid-template-columns:96px 1fr 78px;align-items:center;\n    gap:10px;margin-bottom:10px}\n  #mtpfx51 .save{background:var(--panel2)!important;border:1px solid var(--line)!important;\n    border-left:3px solid var(--clay)!important;border-radius:8px;padding:12px 14px;\n    font-size:13px;line-height:1.6;color:#F0EEE6!important}\n  #mtpfx51 .save b{color:var(--clay)!important;font-size:17px;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n\n  #mtpfx51 .rt{position:relative;height:132px;margin:6px 0 12px}\n  #mtpfx51 .dot{position:absolute;width:11px;height:11px;border-radius:50%;\n    background:var(--clay)!important;left:6%;top:60px;box-shadow:0 0 12px var(--clay);\n    transition:left .85s ease,top .85s ease}\n  #mtpfx51 .verdict{font-size:13px;line-height:1.65;background:var(--panel2)!important;\n    border:1px solid var(--line)!important;border-radius:10px;padding:13px;color:#F0EEE6!important}\n  #mtpfx51 .verdict b{color:var(--clay)!important}\n\n  #mtpfx51 .foot{margin-top:14px;font-size:11px;color:#A29C92!important;display:flex;\n    justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}\n  #mtpfx51 .foot a{color:var(--clay)!important;text-decoration:none}\n  #mtpfx51 hr,#mtpfx51 p:empty,#mtpfx51 del,#mtpfx51 s{display:none!important}\n  @media (max-width:640px){\n    #mtpfx51 .fx{padding:16px 12px}\n    #mtpfx51 .hd h2{font-size:18px}\n    #mtpfx51 .gates{grid-template-columns:1fr}\n    #mtpfx51 .row{grid-template-columns:88px 1fr 46px;gap:7px}\n    #mtpfx51 .cmp{grid-template-columns:76px 1fr 66px;gap:7px}\n    #mtpfx51 .tab{padding:7px 10px;font-size:11.5px}\n  }\n  @media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){\n    #mtpfx51 *{animation:none!important;transition:none!important}\n  }\n&lt;/style&gt;\n&lt;/head&gt;\n&lt;body id=&quot;mtpfx51&quot;&gt;\n&lt;div class=&quot;fx&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;div class=&quot;hd&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h2&gt;Claude Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1, explained&lt;/h2&gt;\n    &lt;p&gt;Four things practitioners need before migrating. Every number below comes from Anthropic's launch post and the Claude Platform docs.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;tabs&quot; role=&quot;tablist&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; role=&quot;tab&quot; aria-selected=&quot;true&quot; data-p=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;One model, two gates&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; role=&quot;tab&quot; aria-selected=&quot;false&quot; data-p=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;Benchmarks&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; role=&quot;tab&quot; aria-selected=&quot;false&quot; data-p=&quot;p3&quot;&gt;Cache-read math&lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;button class=&quot;tab&quot; role=&quot;tab&quot; aria-selected=&quot;false&quot; data-p=&quot;p4&quot;&gt;Safeguard routing&lt;/button&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;pane on&quot; id=&quot;p1&quot; role=&quot;tabpanel&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 are the same weights&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;The only difference is the safeguard layer wrapped around them. Tap a gate to see what changes.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;svg class=&quot;wire&quot; viewBox=&quot;0 0 700 150&quot; preserveAspectRatio=&quot;xMidYMid meet&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;rect x=&quot;250&quot; y=&quot;12&quot; width=&quot;200&quot; height=&quot;40&quot; rx=&quot;8&quot; fill=&quot;#252320&quot; stroke=&quot;#38342E&quot;/&gt;\n      &lt;text x=&quot;350&quot; y=&quot;37&quot; fill=&quot;#F0EEE6&quot; font-size=&quot;14&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot; font-family=&quot;Helvetica,Arial&quot;&gt;Shared model weights&lt;/text&gt;\n      &lt;path class=&quot;flow&quot; d=&quot;M330 52 L170 102&quot; stroke=&quot;#D97757&quot; stroke-width=&quot;2&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot;/&gt;\n      &lt;path class=&quot;flow&quot; d=&quot;M370 52 L530 102&quot; stroke=&quot;#D97757&quot; stroke-width=&quot;2&quot; fill=&quot;none&quot;/&gt;\n      &lt;rect x=&quot;60&quot; y=&quot;102&quot; width=&quot;220&quot; height=&quot;38&quot; rx=&quot;8&quot; fill=&quot;#252320&quot; stroke=&quot;#D97757&quot;/&gt;\n      &lt;text x=&quot;170&quot; y=&quot;126&quot; fill=&quot;#F0EEE6&quot; font-size=&quot;13&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot; font-family=&quot;Helvetica,Arial&quot;&gt;Production safeguards&lt;/text&gt;\n      &lt;rect x=&quot;420&quot; y=&quot;102&quot; width=&quot;220&quot; height=&quot;38&quot; rx=&quot;8&quot; fill=&quot;#252320&quot; stroke=&quot;#D97757&quot;/&gt;\n      &lt;text x=&quot;530&quot; y=&quot;126&quot; fill=&quot;#F0EEE6&quot; font-size=&quot;13&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot; font-family=&quot;Helvetica,Arial&quot;&gt;Trusted-access safeguards&lt;/text&gt;\n    &lt;/svg&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;gates&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;gate&quot; aria-pressed=&quot;true&quot; data-g=&quot;fable&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;Claude Fable 5.1&lt;/b&gt;\n        &lt;span&gt;Generally available. API id claude-fable-5-1.&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;/button&gt;\n      &lt;button class=&quot;gate&quot; aria-pressed=&quot;false&quot; data-g=&quot;mythos&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;b&gt;Claude Mythos 5.1&lt;/b&gt;\n        &lt;span&gt;Project Glasswing participants only.&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;/button&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;detail&quot; id=&quot;d1&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;pane&quot; id=&quot;p2&quot; role=&quot;tabpanel&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Reported scores, Anthropic's own evaluation harness&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;Pick a benchmark. Bars are drawn to a 100-point scale except GDPval-AA v2, which is a rating.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;chips&quot; id=&quot;bchips&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div id=&quot;bars&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot; id=&quot;bnote&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;pane&quot; id=&quot;p3&quot; role=&quot;tabpanel&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;Where the 25 to 45 percent saving comes from&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;Base input stays at $10 per million tokens. Cache reads drop from $1.00 to $0.25 per million. Move the slider to the share of input tokens your agent serves from cache.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;slab&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;Input tokens read from cache&lt;/span&gt;&lt;b id=&quot;pct&quot;&gt;85%&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;input type=&quot;range&quot; id=&quot;sl&quot; min=&quot;0&quot; max=&quot;95&quot; value=&quot;85&quot; step=&quot;5&quot; aria-label=&quot;Share of input tokens read from cache&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cmp&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nm&quot;&gt;Fable 5&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;fill&quot; id=&quot;f5&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;val&quot; id=&quot;v5&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;cmp&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nm&quot;&gt;Fable 5.1&lt;/span&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;track&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;fill lead&quot; id=&quot;f51&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;val&quot; id=&quot;v51&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;save&quot;&gt;Input spend falls &lt;b id=&quot;sv&quot;&gt;&lt;/b&gt; at this cache-hit rate.&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;note&quot;&gt;Input-token cost only, per million input tokens. Output is unchanged at $50 per million on both models, so blended savings on a real workload will be smaller. Anthropic reports roughly 25 percent lower cost on typical workloads and up to about 45 percent on highly agentic ones.&lt;/p&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;pane&quot; id=&quot;p4&quot; role=&quot;tabpanel&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;h3&gt;What Fable 5.1 answers, and what it hands to Opus&lt;/h3&gt;\n    &lt;p class=&quot;sub&quot;&gt;Tap a request and watch where the safeguard layer sends it.&lt;/p&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;chips&quot; id=&quot;rchips&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;rt&quot;&gt;\n      &lt;svg viewBox=&quot;0 0 700 132&quot; preserveAspectRatio=&quot;none&quot; style=&quot;width:100%;height:132px&quot; aria-hidden=&quot;true&quot;&gt;\n        &lt;rect x=&quot;230&quot; y=&quot;48&quot; width=&quot;150&quot; height=&quot;36&quot; rx=&quot;8&quot; fill=&quot;#252320&quot; stroke=&quot;#38342E&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;305&quot; y=&quot;70&quot; fill=&quot;#A29C92&quot; font-size=&quot;12&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot; font-family=&quot;Helvetica,Arial&quot;&gt;Safeguard classifier&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;rect x=&quot;470&quot; y=&quot;8&quot; width=&quot;200&quot; height=&quot;34&quot; rx=&quot;8&quot; fill=&quot;#252320&quot; stroke=&quot;#38342E&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;570&quot; y=&quot;30&quot; fill=&quot;#A29C92&quot; font-size=&quot;12&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot; font-family=&quot;Helvetica,Arial&quot;&gt;Fable 5.1 answers&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;rect x=&quot;470&quot; y=&quot;90&quot; width=&quot;200&quot; height=&quot;34&quot; rx=&quot;8&quot; fill=&quot;#252320&quot; stroke=&quot;#38342E&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;text x=&quot;570&quot; y=&quot;112&quot; fill=&quot;#A29C92&quot; font-size=&quot;12&quot; text-anchor=&quot;middle&quot; font-family=&quot;Helvetica,Arial&quot;&gt;Redirected to Opus&lt;/text&gt;\n        &lt;path d=&quot;M60 66 L230 66&quot; stroke=&quot;#38342E&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;path d=&quot;M380 60 L470 25&quot; stroke=&quot;#38342E&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot;/&gt;\n        &lt;path d=&quot;M380 72 L470 107&quot; stroke=&quot;#38342E&quot; stroke-width=&quot;1.5&quot;/&gt;\n      &lt;/svg&gt;\n      &lt;div class=&quot;dot&quot; id=&quot;dot&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;/div&gt;\n    &lt;div class=&quot;verdict&quot; id=&quot;rv&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n\n  &lt;div class=&quot;foot&quot;&gt;\n    &lt;span&gt;Sources: Anthropic launch post and Claude Platform docs, September 2026.&lt;/span&gt;\n    &lt;span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.marktechpost.com/&quot;&gt;Built by Marktechpost&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n  &lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n\n&lt;script&gt;\n(function(){\n  var $=function(s){return document.querySelector(s)};\n  var tabs=document.querySelectorAll('#mtpfx51 .tab');\n  tabs.forEach(function(t){\n    t.addEventListener('click',function(){\n      tabs.forEach(function(x){x.setAttribute('aria-selected','false')});\n      document.querySelectorAll('#mtpfx51 .pane').forEach(function(p){p.classList.remove('on')});\n      t.setAttribute('aria-selected','true');\n      document.getElementById(t.dataset.p).classList.add('on');\n      if(t.dataset.p==='p2') draw();\n      resize();\n    });\n  });\n\n  var G={\n    fable:'&lt;b&gt;Generally available on the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, Google Cloud and Microsoft Foundry.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;'+\n      '&lt;li&gt;Safety classifiers on. A declined request returns HTTP 200 with stop_reason &quot;refusal&quot;.&lt;/li&gt;'+\n      '&lt;li&gt;Permitted fallback targets are Claude Opus 4.8 and Claude Opus 5.&lt;/li&gt;'+\n      '&lt;li&gt;Now cleared to find software vulnerabilities, but not to develop exploits for them.&lt;/li&gt;'+\n      '&lt;li&gt;Life-sciences R&amp;amp;D queries still route to Opus.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;',\n    mythos:'&lt;b&gt;Restricted to vetted organisations under Project Glasswing, currently US only.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;'+\n      '&lt;li&gt;Same capabilities, safeguards tuned for cyberdefence and life-sciences work.&lt;/li&gt;'+\n      '&lt;li&gt;Reached 60.9% on Terminal-Bench 4.0 against 55.8% for Fable 5.1. The gap is safeguard interventions, not capability.&lt;/li&gt;'+\n      '&lt;li&gt;Routes through the Cyber Verification Program and the Life Sciences Verification Program.&lt;/li&gt;'+\n      '&lt;li&gt;Also powers Claude Security, Anthropic\\u2019s codebase-scanning product.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;'\n  };\n  var gates=document.querySelectorAll('#mtpfx51 .gate');\n  gates.forEach(function(g){\n    g.addEventListener('click',function(){\n      gates.forEach(function(x){x.setAttribute('aria-pressed','false')});\n      g.setAttribute('aria-pressed','true');\n      $('#d1').innerHTML=G[g.dataset.g];resize();\n    });\n  });\n  $('#d1').innerHTML=G.fable;\n\n  var B=[\n   {k:'Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1',max:100,u:'%',\n    d:[['Fable 5.1',52.6],['Opus 5',29.0],['Fable 5',24.7],['GPT-5.6 Sol',22.4]],\n    n:'Agentic scientific research. Anthropic reports a standard error of 3.5 to 4.5 points per model.'},\n   {k:'Terminal-Bench 4.0',max:100,u:'%',\n    d:[['Mythos 5.1',60.9],['Fable 5.1',55.8],['Opus 5',52.3],['Fable 5',42.0],['GPT-5.6 Sol',37.3]],\n    n:'Agentic coding. Mythos 5.1 is the same model with fewer safeguard interventions.'},\n   {k:'CursorBench 3.2.0',max:100,u:'%',\n    d:[['Fable 5.1',73.4],['Fable 5',70.5],['Opus 5',70.0],['GPT-5.6 Sol',67.2]],\n    n:'Agentic coding, measured at max effort.'},\n   {k:&quot;Humanity's Last Exam&quot;,max:100,u:'%',\n    d:[['Fable 5.1',60.9],['Fable 5',57.8],['Opus 5',56.6]],\n    n:'Multidisciplinary reasoning, no tools. With tools: 65.0, 63.8 and 63.6 respectively. No GPT-5.6 Sol figure published.'},\n   {k:'AutomationBench',max:100,u:'%',\n    d:[['Fable 5.1',31.4],['Opus 5',26.9],['GPT-5.6 Sol',19.6],['Fable 5',17.1]],\n    n:'Business workflows. Fable 5 scored zero on tasks where its safeguards intervened.'},\n   {k:'OSWorld 2.0 (strict)',max:100,u:'%',\n    d:[['Fable 5.1',41.7],['Opus 5',39.6],['Fable 5',36.1]],\n    n:'Computer use. Partial-credit scores are 77.9, 75.4 and 72.9. Scores use the August 2026 task release and are not comparable with earlier OSWorld 2.0 results.'},\n   {k:'GDPval-AA v2',max:2000,u:'',\n    d:[['Fable 5.1',1853],['Opus 5',1824],['Fable 5',1723],['GPT-5.6 Sol',1711]],\n    n:'Knowledge work. A rating, not a percentage, so bars are scaled to 2000.'}\n  ];\n  var cur=0, cw=$('#bchips');\n  B.forEach(function(b,i){\n    var c=document.createElement('button');\n    c.className='chip';c.type='button';c.textContent=b.k;\n    c.setAttribute('aria-pressed',i===0?'true':'false');\n    c.addEventListener('click',function(){\n      cur=i;\n      cw.querySelectorAll('.chip').forEach(function(x,j){x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',j===i?'true':'false')});\n      draw();\n    });\n    cw.appendChild(c);\n  });\n  function draw(){\n    var b=B[cur],h='';\n    b.d.forEach(function(r){\n      h+='&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;nm&quot;&gt;'+r[0]+'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;track&quot;&gt;'+\n         '&lt;div class=&quot;fill'+(/Fable 5\\.1|Mythos 5\\.1/.test(r[0])?' lead':'')+'&quot; data-w=&quot;'+\n         (r[1]/b.max*100)+'&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;val&quot;&gt;'+r[1]+b.u+'&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;';\n    });\n    $('#bars').innerHTML=h;$('#bnote').textContent=b.n;\n    requestAnimationFrame(function(){\n      document.querySelectorAll('#mtpfx51 #bars .fill').forEach(function(f){f.style.width=f.dataset.w+'%'});\n    });\n    resize();\n  }\n  draw();\n\n  var sl=$('#sl');\n  function calc(){\n    var c=+sl.value/100;\n    var a=(1-c)*10+c*1.00, b=(1-c)*10+c*0.25;\n    $('#pct').textContent=sl.value+'%';\n    $('#v5').textContent='$'+a.toFixed(2);$('#v51').textContent='$'+b.toFixed(2);\n    $('#f5').style.width=(a/10*100)+'%';$('#f51').style.width=(b/10*100)+'%';\n    $('#sv').textContent=((1-b/a)*100).toFixed(1)+'%';\n  }\n  sl.addEventListener('input',calc);calc();\n\n  var R=[\n   {t:'Ask an elementary biology question',ok:1,\n    v:'&lt;b&gt;Answered.&lt;/b&gt; Anthropic says the latest biology safeguards fire 85% less often on benign elementary biology and medical questions than the ones that shipped with Fable 5.'},\n   {t:'Find a vulnerability in my codebase',ok:1,\n    v:'&lt;b&gt;Answered, and this is new in 5.1.&lt;/b&gt; Fable 5.1 is now allowed to identify software vulnerabilities. Claude Code users should see about 60% fewer cyber-safeguard interventions per session.'},\n   {t:'Write a working exploit for it',ok:0,\n    v:'&lt;b&gt;Redirected to Opus.&lt;/b&gt; Vulnerability discovery is permitted; exploit development is not.'},\n   {t:'Run a penetration test',ok:0,\n    v:'&lt;b&gt;Redirected to Opus.&lt;/b&gt; Penetration testing stays on the dual-use list, alongside binary-based vulnerability scanning.'},\n   {t:'Life-sciences R&amp;D work',ok:0,\n    v:'&lt;b&gt;Redirected to Opus.&lt;/b&gt; Research and development queries in the life sciences still go to Opus models. Vetted professionals get these capabilities through Mythos 5.1 under the Life Sciences Verification Program.'}\n  ];\n  var rw=$('#rchips');\n  R.forEach(function(r,i){\n    var c=document.createElement('button');\n    c.className='chip';c.type='button';c.textContent=r.t;\n    c.setAttribute('aria-pressed',i===0?'true':'false');\n    c.addEventListener('click',function(){\n      rw.querySelectorAll('.chip').forEach(function(x,j){x.setAttribute('aria-pressed',j===i?'true':'false')});\n      route(i);\n    });\n    rw.appendChild(c);\n  });\n  function route(i){\n    var d=$('#dot');d.style.left='6%';d.style.top='60px';\n    setTimeout(function(){d.style.left='42%';},30);\n    setTimeout(function(){d.style.left='78%';d.style.top=R[i].ok?'20px':'100px';},700);\n    $('#rv').innerHTML=R[i].v;resize();\n  }\n  route(0);\n\n  function resize(){\n    try{parent.postMessage({fxHeight:document.body.offsetHeight+40},'*')}catch(e){}\n  }\n  window.addEventListener('load',resize);\n  setTimeout(resize,250);setTimeout(resize,900);\n})();\n&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;/body&gt;\n&lt;/html&gt;\n\" scrolling=\"no\" title=\"Claude Fable 5.1 interactive explainer\" loading=\"lazy\"></iframe>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <h2 id=\"h-key-takeaways\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></h2>\n  <ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n   <li>Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1 are one model behind two safeguard layers; only Fable is generally available.</li>\n   <li>52.6% on Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1, roughly double Fable 5’s 24.7%.</li>\n   <li>Cache reads fall 75% to $0.25 per million; base rates are untouched.</li>\n   <li>Three breaking API changes hit any agent that edits conversation history.</li>\n   <li>30-day retention applies; zero data retention needs express authorization.</li>\n  </ul>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Check out the&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.anthropic.com/claude-fable-and-mythos-5-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Technical Details</a></strong>.<strong>&nbsp;</strong>Also,&nbsp;feel free to follow us on&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://x.com/intent/follow?screen_name=marktechpost\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Twitter</mark></a></strong>&nbsp;and don’t forget to join our&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/machinelearningnews/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">150k+ML SubReddit</a></strong>&nbsp;and Subscribe to&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://www.aidevsignals.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">our Newsletter</a></strong>. Wait! are you on telegram?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://t.me/machinelearningresearchnews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">now you can join us on telegram as well.</a></strong></p>\n  <p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Need to partner with us for promoting your GitHub Repo OR Hugging Face Page OR Product Release OR Webinar etc.?&nbsp;<strong><a href=\"https://forms.gle/wbash1wF6efRj8G58\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><mark>Connect with us</mark></a></strong></p>\n  <!-- MOLONGUI AUTHORSHIP PLUGIN 5.2.11 -->\n  <!-- https://www.molongui.com/wordpress-plugin-post-authors -->\n  <div class=\"m-a-box \" data-box-layout=\"slim\" data-box-position=\"below\" data-multiauthor=\"false\" data-author-id=\"1\" data-author-type=\"user\" data-author-archived=\"\">\n   <div class=\"m-a-box-container\">\n    <div class=\"m-a-box-tab m-a-box-content m-a-box-profile\" data-profile-layout=\"layout-1\" data-author-ref=\"user-1\" itemscope itemid=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\" itemtype=\"https://schema.org/Person\">\n     <div class=\"m-a-box-content-middle\">\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-avatar\" data-source=\"local\">\n       <a class=\"m-a-box-avatar-url\" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-150x150.png\" class=\"avatar avatar-150 photo\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-150x150.png 150w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-80x80.png 80w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-24x24.png 24w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-48x48.png 48w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-96x96.png 96w, https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM-300x300.png 300w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" data-attachment-id=\"17663\" data-permalink=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/?attachment_id=17663\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM.png\" data-orig-size=\"832,778\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-meta=\"{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}\" data-image-title=\"Screen Shot 2021-09-14 at 9.02.24 AM\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-large-file=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/06/Screen-Shot-2021-09-14-at-9.02.24-AM.png\"></a>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-social \">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-facebook m-ico-\" href=\"https://www.facebook.com/MarkTechPost/\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Facebook profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-facebook\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-twitter m-ico-\" href=\"https://twitter.com/asifrazzaq1988\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Twitter profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-twitter\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-social-icon m-a-list-social-icon\">\n        <a class=\"m-icon-container m-ico-linkedin m-ico-\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/asifrazzaq/\" target=\"_self\" itemprop=\"sameAs\" aria-label=\"View Asif Razzaq's Linkedin profile\"><i class=\"m-a-icon-linkedin\"></i></a>\n       </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-data\">\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-name\">\n        <h5 itemprop=\"name\"><a class=\"m-a-box-name-url \" href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com/author/6flvq/\" itemprop=\"url\"> Asif Razzaq</a></h5>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-item m-a-box-meta\">\n        <a href=\"https://www.marktechpost.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-web\">Website</span></a>&nbsp;<span class=\"m-a-box-meta-divider\">|</span>&nbsp; <a href=\"#\" class=\"m-a-box-data-toggle\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span class=\"m-a-box-string-more-posts\">+ posts</span></a>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-bio\" itemprop=\"description\">\n        <p>Asif Razzaq is the CEO of Marktechpost Media Inc.. As a visionary entrepreneur and engineer, Asif is committed to harnessing the potential of Artificial Intelligence for social good. His most recent endeavor is the launch of an Artificial Intelligence Media Platform, Marktechpost, which stands out for its in-depth coverage of machine learning and deep learning news that is both technically sound and easily understandable by a wide audience. The platform boasts of over 2 million monthly views, illustrating its popularity among audiences.</p>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"m-a-box-related\" data-related-layout=\"layout-1\"></div>\n      </div>\n     </div>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <!-- CONTENT END 2 -->\n </body>\n</html>",
  "aiSummary": "Anthropic 发布了 Claude Fable 5.1 和 Mythos 5.1，其科学智能体性能实现巨大飞跃（Terminal-Bench-Science 评分 52.6%），且缓存读取成本降低了 75%。",
  "oneSentenceSummary": "Anthropic 发布了 Claude Fable 5.1 和 Mythos 5.1，其科学智能体性能实现巨大飞跃（Terminal-Bench-Science 评分 52.6%），且缓存读取成本降低了 75%。",
  "summary": "Anthropic 推出了 Claude Fable 5.1（通用可用）和 Claude Mythos 5.1（受限可用），两者共享相同的底层模型，但安全防护层有所不同。此次更新在科学研究任务中带来了显著的性能提升，在 Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1 上得分 52.6%，几乎是前代产品的两倍。在商业方面，缓存读取价格下降 75% 至每百万 token 0.25 美元，使智能体工作负载的成本最高降低 45%。此次发布还引入了关于工具调用、思考块兼容性和对话历史编辑的三个关键 API 破坏性变更，并更新了针对网络安全和生物研究的安全防护措施。",
  "mainPoints": [
    {
      "point": "科学推理能力的显著飞跃",
      "explanation": "Fable 5.1 在 Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1 上达到了 52.6% 的得分，显著优于 Fable 5 (24.7%) 和 GPT-5.6 Sol (22.4%)，证明了其在智能体科学研究方面的能力增强。"
    },
    {
      "point": "缓存读取成本大幅降低",
      "explanation": "缓存读取价格从每百万 token 1.00 美元降至 0.25 美元。Anthropic 估计，这将使典型工作负载的成本降低 25%，而对于上下文密集型的智能体工作流，成本最高可降低 45%。"
    },
    {
      "point": "关键的 API 破坏性变更",
      "explanation": "开发者必须适应强制工具调用 (`tool_choice: any/tool`) 的移除、思考块与模型绑定的特性（导致路由器无法向下兼容），以及编辑早期对话轮次时出现的新错误。"
    },
    {
      "point": "精细化的安全防护层",
      "explanation": "Fable 与 Mythos 的区别在于安全防护层；新更新允许漏洞发现（但不允许开发漏洞利用工具），并将生物安全防护中对良性请求的误触发率降低了 85%。"
    }
  ],
  "keyQuotes": [
    "「核心能力指标是 Terminal-Bench-Science 0.1 上的 52.6%，而 Fable 5 为 24.7%，Opus 5 为 29.0%。」",
    "「缓存读取成本下降 75%，从每百万 token 1.00 美元降至 0.25 美元，相对于基础输入仅为 0.025 倍，而其他所有 Claude 模型均为 0.1 倍。」",
    "「两个相同模型之间的差距在于安全干预的成本，这是一个异常坦诚的披露。」"
  ],
  "tags": [
    "Model Releases",
    "Anthropic",
    "LLM",
    "AI Engineering",
